# COMPREHENSIVE HTML REFERENCE & NOTES

# Excalidraw Data

## Text Elements
HTML5 COMPREHENSIVE REFERENCE & CHEAT SHEET ^headerTitle

1. DOCUMENT STRUCTURE ^secStructure

<!DOCTYPE html> - Declares HTML5 document type
<html> - Root element of the HTML page
<head> - Contains metadata, title, linked CSS/scripts
<title> - Document title (shown in browser tab)
<meta charset="UTF-8"> - Character encoding
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"> - Responsive viewport setup
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"> - External CSS link
<script src="script.js" defer></script> - External JavaScript execution
<body> - Visible page content container
 ^txtStructureDetails

2. SEMANTIC LAYOUT TAGS ^secSemantic

<header> - Intro content, nav bar, or header banner
<nav> - Container for primary navigation links
<main> - Unique main content of the document (1 per page)
<section> - Standalone section grouping related content
<article> - Self-contained composition (blog post, news item)
<aside> - Sidebar or content indirectly related to main text
<footer> - Page footer (copyright, contact info, secondary links)
<figure> / <figcaption> - Self-contained media & caption
 ^txtSemanticDetails

3. TEXT & CONTENT FORMATTING ^secTextFormatting

<h1> to <h6> - Headings (H1 is primary, H6 lowest priority)
<p> - Paragraph text block
<a href="URL" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> - Anchor hyperlink
<strong> - Important text (default bold style)
<em> - Emphasized text (default italic style)
<span> - Generic inline text container
<mark> - Highlighted text
<code> - Inline code snippet
<pre> - Preformatted text (preserves whitespace/newlines)
<blockquote> - Block quote from an external source
<hr> - Thematic break / horizontal rule
<br> - Line break
 ^txtTextDetails

4. LISTS & TABLES ^secListsTables

-- LISTS --
<ul> - Unordered list (bullet points)
<ol type="1"> - Ordered list (numbered/lettered)
<li> - List item

-- TABLES --
<table> - Wrapper for tabular data
<thead> - Table header row group
<tbody> - Main table body data group
<tfoot> - Table summary/footer group
<tr> - Table row
<th> - Header cell (bold & centered by default)
<td> - Standard data cell
colspan="2" / rowspan="2" - Merge columns / rows
 ^txtListsTablesDetails

5. FORMS & USER INPUT ^secForms

<form action="/submit" method="POST"> - Form wrapper

-- INPUT TYPES --
<input type="text" placeholder="Enter name">
<input type="password"> | <input type="email">
<input type="number" min="0" max="100">
<input type="checkbox"> | <input type="radio" name="group">
<input type="file"> | <input type="color">
<input type="date"> | <input type="hidden">

-- OTHER CONTROLS --
<label for="id"> - Accessible label linked via input ID
<textarea rows="4" cols="50"> - Multi-line text field
<select name="choice"> / <option value="1"> - Dropdown list
<button type="submit"> - Trigger button
 ^txtFormsDetails

6. MEDIA, EMBEDS & INTERACTIVE ^secMedia

<img src="path.jpg" alt="Description" loading="lazy"> - Image
<audio controls src="audio.mp3"></audio> - Audio player
<video controls width="600" poster="thumb.jpg">
  <source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
</video>
<iframe> - Embed external webpage/video
<canvas> - Scriptable rendering for 2D/3D graphics
<svg> - Vector graphics container
<details> / <summary> - Native collapsible accordion
<dialog open> - Native popup modal window
 ^txtMediaDetails

7. ATTRIBUTES & BEST PRACTICES ^secBestPractices

-- GLOBAL ATTRIBUTES --
id="..." - Unique element identifier
class="..." - CSS/JS styling selector class
style="..." - Inline CSS styles
title="..." - Hover tooltip text
data-*="..." - Custom data attributes for JS
hidden - Hides element from DOM rendering
tabindex="0" - Keyboard navigation order

-- ACCESSIBILITY (a11y) & SEO --
• Always provide descriptive 'alt' text on <img>
• Use semantic tags over generic <div> for screen readers
• Ensure proper heading hierarchy (H1 -> H2 -> H3)
• Use aria-* attributes when building custom UI controls
 ^txtBestPracticesDetails

